cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use FDP-1, please cite the specification using these metadata."
title: "FDP-1: Food Data Provenance Declaration"
abstract: >-
  FDP-1 is a minimal, RFC-style specification for declaring the provenance of a
  nutrient value (seven fields, including a coded nutrient identity) and the
  validation status of any score computed from such values (five fields, including
  a weakest-link provenance rule). It does not score food; it wraps any existing
  scoring system without modification. Archived with a dependency-free reference
  validator and a worked example. Status: Draft / Request for Comments.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Murff
    given-names: Paul
    affiliation: "Morf Engineering"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-07-26"
license: Apache-2.0
